<title>USA: Northrop gets Boeing contract.</title>
<headline>Northrop gets Boeing contract.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp. said Monday it received a contract from Boeing Co. worth more than $200 million to make parts for Boeing jetliners.</p>
<p>The new work includes fan cowl assemblies, composite thrust reverser and inlet panels and other composite components.</p>
<p>Northrop stock rose 37.5 cents to $83.25 in afternoon trading on the New York Stock Exchange, and Boeing was 50 cents higher at $57.875.</p>
